# November 24, 2026: Carnegie libraries of western and central New York, the first batch of a pass asked for by the
# owner to put the buildings Andrew Carnegie paid for on the map. Started from Wikipedia's "List of Carnegie libraries
# in New York" (107 public libraries from 42 grants; 66 of them in New York City, listed separately and left for a later
# batch). This batch: the 20 outside New York City in the west, the Southern Tier and round Syracuse that the Atlas did
# not have. Sources opened in this session: Wikipedia as raw text (tools/wiki_raw.py), and through the web fetch tool the
# libraries' own pages (hours), the Buffalo and Erie County Public Library, local historical pages and newspapers.
# Pins: ArcGIS geocoder points for the street addresses the list gives, looked at on the leaf-off aerial.
