  'Andover\'s library was built with $5,000 from Andrew Carnegie, granted in November 1911. Otis Dockstader of Elmira drew it as a fireproof one-storey building, 47 by 34 feet, over a basement assembly room. The local paper reported its opening reception in May 1913; Wikipedia\'s list of Carnegie libraries gives 1912, so the year it opened is not settled.',
