  'A small Mission-style library, 48 by 32 feet, built in 1910 and 1911 with $5,000 from Andrew Carnegie (granted April 1909) to plans by E. F. Prichell. It was listed on the National Register in 2003, and a recent renovation added a lift and a ramp and steadied the front wall.',
  'Cream brick under a red clay tile roof, with an arched entrance and leaded-glass windows. Inside, the old circulation desk and table were restored and kept, and framed photographs show the foyer and stair as they were before the lift. A National Register marker stands at Main and Olean Streets.',
