N('old-olean-library','Old Olean Library (Carnegie library, now a restaurant)','Olean','wny','civic','standing',42.07694,-78.43033,'exact','view','walk','','1909–1910',
  'Olean\'s Carnegie library was drawn by Edward L. Tilton in the Beaux-Arts style. Carnegie gave $40,000 of its cost; the cornerstone was laid on July 3, 1909, and it opened on May 23, 1910. The library moved to a former supermarket in 1973, and from about 1982 the building has been The Old Library Restaurant. It was listed on the National Register in 1985.',
  'Buff pressed brick with terra cotta trim. Inside: the grand stair, the central atrium, original bookcases and two fireplaces (the carved mahogany bar came later, from a Chicago steakhouse). The restaurant was sold in August 2025 and a local paper said it would reopen late in 2025; whether it is open now was not checked. A "Former Library" marker stands at the site.',
  '','Privately owned restaurant, in the Union and State Streets Historic District downtown. Seen from South Union Street at any time; inside only as a customer, when it is open. Hours not checked.',
  [W('Olean Public Library'),['William G. Pomeroy Foundation: Former Library marker','https://www.wgpfoundation.org/historic-markers/former-library/'],['Olean Times Herald, October 16, 2025: Old Library sold','https://www.oleantimesherald.com/2025/10/16/ellicottville-depot-property-purchase-largest-september-old-library-sold'],['The Villager, October 29, 2025: reopening plans','https://thevillagerny.com/2025/10/29/old-library-inn-olean-celebrates-new-ownership-to-reopen-before-2026']],
  conf='mixed',brick='no',hours=''),
