  'Dunkirk\'s library was built with $25,000 from Andrew Carnegie. Its cornerstone was laid on November 5, 1904, and the library moved in on February 17, 1906. The main block is 64 by 75 feet with a half-round extension at the back, and the top of its dome stood 42 feet high.',
