  'A two-storey Classical Revival library built in 1902 with $10,000 from Andrew Carnegie, granted in January 1902; the library itself gives about 1903. Wikipedia names Archimedes Russell and Funda and Del Monico Brothers as its architect and builders. It was listed on the National Register in 1986.',
